// W5-24 U3a/t, S-600 (spec §18.1: "`@` の属性の修正候補は、その属性を可視性と `rt` の前（既にある属性の後ろ）へ移す形である"): the E0002 of an attribute after `pub` of a
// method of an `impl` (`pub @fp(relaxed) fn a(self)` is `@fp(relaxed) pub fn a(self)`) has one candidate, which writes the
// attribute before the visibility of the member, and the file has no error left after it (`clean`, S-253). The main position is
// the attribute. A file with one unit, so that `clean` looks at the whole file.

pub struct Pt {
  x: F32,
}

impl Pt {
  @fp(relaxed) pub fn a(self) -> F32 {              //~ E0002
    self.x
  }
}
